<ProseLayout
  title="Terms of service"
  metaTitle="Pilot terms | PumpOS"
  description="Draft terms for the PumpOS guided pilot."
  path="/legal/terms"
  eyebrow="PumpOS pilot"
  noindex
>
  <Card as="aside" class="prose-callout" role="note">
    Draft, pending founder approval and legal review. This page is not a service agreement and has no effective date yet.
  </Card>
  <h2>Scope of the pilot</h2>
  <p>The pilot is a guided rollout for selected fuel stations. We agree with you in advance which capabilities are included. Planned capabilities are not part of the pilot unless we confirm them in writing.</p>
  <h2>Onboarding and support</h2>
  <p>We help set up your station and users. Support channels and response times are to be decided and will be stated before you join.</p>
  <h2>Pricing, payment and cancellation</h2>
  <p>Pricing is agreed with each station before it joins. Payment terms, refunds and cancellation arrangements are not yet settled.</p>
  <h2>Account responsibilities</h2>
  <p>Your organization is responsible for the users it adds, keeping credentials secure, and the accuracy of the records it enters.</p>
  <h2>Service limitations</h2>
  <p>PumpOS works online. It is not a point-of-sale system or an accounting package, and extended offline operation is not part of the pilot.</p>
  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>Your station's operational records remain yours. Export and deletion arrangements on termination are to be decided; see the <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy information</a>.</p>
  <h2>Termination and liability</h2>
  <p>Termination rights and limits on liability will be set out in the final terms after legal review.</p>
  <h2>Demonstrations</h2>
  <p>The website's walkthroughs use illustrative sample data.</p>
  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@pumpos.app?subject=Pilot%20terms">hello@pumpos.app</a> to discuss the terms for your station.</p>
  <h2>Open items before publication</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Legal operator name and jurisdiction.</li>
    <li>Pricing, payment, refund and cancellation terms.</li>
    <li>Support scope and response times.</li>
    <li>Data export and deletion on termination.</li>
    <li>Liability and termination wording, after legal review.</li>
    <li>Effective and revision dates.</li>
  </ul>
</ProseLayout>
